# Fleet Hosts assignment scope

This repo automates Fleet Hosts and host details only. Follow this boundary on every change. Do not expand into Design QA, Linear filing, or other product surfaces.

## In scope

- **Hosts** — `http://localhost:1337/hosts/manage` (`/hosts/manage`). Anything that stays on this page.
- **Host details** — the page reached by clicking a host. Tabs stay in scope: `/hosts/:id/details`, `/software/inventory`, `/policies`, `/reports`.
- **Still this page:** the platform/label filter at `/hosts/manage/labels/:id`; modals that do not navigate away (Add hosts, Edit columns, Delete, Enroll secrets); CSV export.
- **Stack** — Playwright with TypeScript. Run against a fresh `fleetctl preview` (defaults in `.env.example`: `` / `REDACTED#`).

## Out of scope

- **Running scripts**, including when the control is on Hosts or host details.
- **The next page after a click.** Label editor, a single policy or query, a software title, script run, settings. Stop at the control that would navigate there. Do not add a page object, spec, or API coverage for that destination.
- Premium or MDM-only controls that free preview cannot exercise. Record them in `COVERAGE.md` as out of scope.

## What to automate

Cover every in-scope control in `fleet-e2e-interaction-coverage.mdc`. Do not add a test for a control that rule marks out of scope.

## Docs and defects

- Keep `README.md` current: how to run, what was automated and why, and what to do next with more time.
- Update `COVERAGE.md` when coverage changes (covered, not covered, and why).
- If AI tools were used, say so in the README.
- File bugs and product questions as GitHub issues in this repo. Do not file them in Linear.

Living record: `README.md` and `COVERAGE.md`.
